quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  2,94,"Say: ‘If the abode of the Hereafter in the sight of Allah is to be for you alone and no one else, then you should long for death (without any fear) if your claim is true.’"
  2,95,"However, they will never long for it because of what their hands have sent ahead. Allah is All-Knowing of the wrongdoers."
  2,96,"Indeed, you will find them ambitious for life more eagerly than any other people, even the polytheists. Each of them would wish to be given a life of a thousand years. Even if their lives were prolonged, it would not save them from the torment. Allah is All-Seeing of what they do."
  2,97,"(O Prophet) say: ‘Whoever is an enemy of Jibril ([Gabriel], should know that) it is he who has brought down the Qur’an on your heart with the command of Allah, confirming the previous scriptures, as a guide and glad tidings for the believers."
  2,98,"Whoever is an enemy of Allah, His angels, His Messengers and Jibril (Gabriel) and Mika’il (Michael), (should know that) Allah is indeed the enemy of such disbelievers.’"
  2,99,"Certainly, We have sent down clear revelations to you; none will deny them except the evildoers."
  2,100,"Is it not so that whenever they make a covenant, some of them cast it away? Rather, most of them do not believe."
  2,101,"And (now) when a Messenger (Muhammad [blessings and peace be upon him]) has come to them from Allah, confirming that which they already had, some of those given the Book (i.e. the Torah) throw the Book of Allah behind their backs, as if they did not know (that it was Allah’s Book)."
